ption after all there is a  ton going on within this seriously  bizarre film is it a Western a horror  movie a satire it has elements of  everything and films that attempt that  sort of genre collage frequently get a  bad rap from critics but if you accept  ravenous for the whacked out horror it  is it's hard not to fall in love with  its oddball mixture of history murder  and pitch black comedy Guy Pearce leads  the cast the second lieutenant Jon  Voight an American soldier fighting in  the mexican-american war the myth though  the Windigo is blended with the story of  the Donner Party set off by a  particularly twisted interpretation of  manifest destiny it's also totally  bonkers but that's the point  ravenous is an overload of American myth  making sure there's a whole lot of  gruesome gore in there but ravenous does  nothing without reason and as a result  easily stands out as one of the  strangest and most satisfying horror  movies of the 1990s fallen is a movie  that definitely combines psychological  horror with the police procedural plots  and manages to pull off a genuinely  wonderful ending to boot and boy were  the critics unimpressed the premise of  fallen seems simple the police catch a  serial killer then have to deal with the  copycats things start to go sideways  when demonic imagery starts to appear  suggesting that there is a lot more  going on with the original killer than  what the police initially thought the  movie is anchored by an awesome cast  including Denzel Washington John Goodman  and Donald Sutherland it's a testament  to their skill that they pull fallen  story off which combines street-level  action with forces of literally biblical  proportions fallen might have seen flat  - critics but revisited today it comes  off as unique self-assured and just the  tiniest bit weird not an easy  combination but fallen pulls it off with  aplomb check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite movies are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single  one  [Music]
 

